        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{6{log}_{8}(2\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\frac{\\log{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{\\log{\\left(8 \\right)}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x \\log{\\left(8 \\right)}}\\,\u27f9\\,\\log{\\left(8 \\right)}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1/3$ | $2/3$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{6{log}_{8}(2\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{12}{5}\\int_{1}^{2}{log}_{8}(2\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{12}{5}\\int_{1/3}^{2/3}u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}8\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{12 \\log{\\left(8 \\right)}}{5}\\int_{1/3}^{2/3}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(6\\operatorname{ln}8\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}\\right)|_{1/3}^{2/3} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(3\\operatorname{ln}8\\cdot (\\frac{4}{9}-\\frac{1}{9})\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\operatorname{ln}8\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
